The Increasing Importance of Judgment 
AI systems may become increasingly capable of performing technical and analytical tasks, but 
organizations will still need people who can determine: 
 what the organization is trying to achieve;  
 whether an AI-generated solution is appropriate;  
 whether its assumptions are reasonable;  
 whether its results can be trusted;  
 and what consequences may result from using it.  
This is particularly important when decisions involve significant financial, legal, organizational, 
or human consequences. As AI capabilities increase, human judgment may become more 
important, because people will increasingly be responsible for deciding when and how AI

potential consequences therefore increase as the system gains authority to act. 
Boundaries and Human Control 
AI agents should therefore operate within clearly defined boundaries. These boundaries may 
specify: 
 which information the agent can access;  
 which applications it can use;  
 which actions it can perform;  
 maximum transaction amounts;  
 which actions require human approval;  
 and when the agent must stop and request assistance.  
This approach allows organizations to obtain some benefits of autonomy without giving the AI 
unrestricted authority. 
Monitoring Agent Behavior 
An autonomous system also needs appropriate monitoring. The organization may need to record: 
 what the agent was asked to accomplish;  
 what information it accessed;

 the importance of the process;  
 the consequences of errors;  
 the information available to the agent;  
 the actions it can perform;  
 the required level of human oversight;  
 and the controls that remain outside the AI system.  
These considerations connect the future development of AI agents directly to the principles of 
architecture, security, governance, and accountability discussed in earlier chapters. 
15.4 Changing Professional Roles in an AI-Enabled Environment 
As AI systems become more capable, they are likely to affect the work of Information Systems 
professionals. The most important change may not be the disappearance of professional roles, but 
a redistribution of responsibilities between people and increasingly capable AI systems.
